course: dictionary
lesson: 8927
title: Sighting: a rare moment of seeing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sighting is a time when someone sees something rare, unusual or wanted, such as a bird, a whale or a missing person. «People still report thylacine sightings, but none have been proven.» Here a sighting is a report that someone saw the animal, not proof that it is really there.
explain: The same spelling can also be a verb form. «Sight» means to see or catch sight of something, so «sighting» is its -ing form. Read the sentence and ask: does it describe an event of seeing something rare? Then sighting is the noun. Could it mean aiming a telescope or gun? Then it is the verb.
explain: Clues help you choose. A noun often comes after a word like «a», «the», «rare» or «reported», as in «a rare sighting» or «reported sightings». Swap in «a time when someone saw it» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A sighting is an occasion when someone sees something rare, unusual or wanted.
fact: Birdwatchers record sightings of birds in a log.
fact: Police ask for sightings of a missing person or animal.
fact: Sighting is also the -ing form of «sight», meaning to see or catch sight of, or to aim a gun or telescope.
fact: Phrases to know: «a rare sighting», «first sighting», «reported sightings», «UFO sighting».
exercise: Scientists count «sightings» to see if animals are rare. What is a sighting? | A loud noise made by an animal | *An occasion when someone sees something rare or unusual | A map of where animals sleep | A kind of gun
exercise: «People still report thylacine sightings, but none have been proven.» What does «sightings» mean here? | *Times people say they saw the animal | Times the zoo closed | Times people counted their sheep | Times the animal was fed at the zoo
exercise: Which word is the -ing form of «sight», meaning to see or catch sight of? | sightseer | sights | *sighting | sightless
test: «Megalodon is extinct: no fresh teeth, bitten whales or sightings are found.» What does this tell us? | There are many megalodons near every coast | *Scientists have no sign that it is still alive | Megalodon is alive and hiding in the sea | Whales have stopped having teeth
test: A child can help nature by recording sightings for scientists. What does «recording sightings» mean? | Drawing pictures of the moon | *Writing down each time they see wild animals | Buying new pets for the house | Cleaning the cages at the zoo
exam: In stories, «UFO sightings» and «ghost sightings» are unproven reports. What does unproven mean? | *Not yet shown to be true | Proved to be false by a scientist | Proved to be true | Written down in a log
